course: dictionary
lesson: 9873
title: The tablespoon: a spoon and a measure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tablespoon is a large spoon used for serving food or for measuring in cooking. Recipes shorten it to tbsp, or sometimes just T.
explain: The second meaning is about amount. «A tablespoon holds about three teaspoons.» Here the word holds tells you that a tablespoon is also a measure: the amount that spoon can carry.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «big spoon» in place of tablespoon in the sentence. In a recipe it would not be enough, because you need the exact amount, not just any big spoon.
fact: A tablespoon is a large spoon for serving food or measuring in cooking.
fact: «Tbsp» is the short form of tablespoon in recipes.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, the USA and New Zealand, a tablespoon is about 15 ml.
fact: In Australia, a tablespoon is 20 ml.
fact: In the UK and the USA, 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons, so «tsp» means teaspoon and «tbsp» means tablespoon.
exercise: «A tablespoon holds about three teaspoons.» How many teaspoons is about one tablespoon in the UK? | *Three | Ten | Two | Five
exercise: A recipe says 2 tbsp of oil. What does tbsp stand for? | Table | Teaspoon | *Tablespoon | Tablet
exercise: What is a tablespoon used for? | Writing letters | Sweeping the floor | *Serving food or measuring in cooking | Playing tennis
test: Medicine comes with its own measuring spoon. Why should you use that spoon, not a kitchen spoon? | Because kitchen spoons are too shiny | Because the medicine tastes better | *So the dose is measured correctly | Because it is bigger
test: A tablespoon is about 15 ml in the UK but 20 ml in one country. Which country uses 20 ml? | Ireland | The USA | *Australia | New Zealand
exam: Why do recipes usually ask for level tablespoons, not heaped ones? | Because heaped spoons are heavier to lift | Because level spoons look neater on the plate | Because heaped spoons break easily | *Because the amount in the recipe is meant to be exact, so a level spoon gives the right result
